> Why should *I*  give money when no one else replies?
>

1) Why should it matter what other people do? If you want Lojban to have a
decent server, you should give money *regardless* of what anyone else does.
2) How do you know no one else has given any money? Did you ever think
maybe the people who've donated merely don't have any need/desire to be
acknowledged for supporting something they care about?

You should give money to improve the server because you want the server to
be improved. If you don't want Lojban to have a better server than it does
currently, then you wouldn't be thinking of buying your own for the
purpose. Since you are, you do want a better server, and as I already said,
your money would be better spent improving the one we have than wasting it
on buying a server no one but you will ever look at.


